      "widgets_values": [
        "Photorealistic premium billiards fashion commercial, vertical 9:16, one continuous shot, no cuts.\n\nUse the uploaded first frame as the exact visual reference. Preserve the adult woman's face, hairstyle, white fitted polo shirt, black pleated skirt, black knee-high socks, body proportions, pool cue and the billiards hall exactly.\n\nThe woman stands beside the pool table holding the cue naturally. During the entire 5-second shot, she performs one simple continuous action: she takes one slow step toward the table, turns her upper body slightly, places her bridge hand on the table edge, leans forward into a natural billiards stance, and calmly aligns the cue toward the white cue ball. She does not hit the ball.\n\nCamera movement is slow and controlled: a smooth gimbal dolly-in from a medium full-body shot to a medium waist-up shot, 35mm cinematic lens, stable horizon, natural perspective. Keep the woman's face and clothing consistent throughout. No camera angle changes, no close-up montage, no sudden zoom, no scene transition.\n\nModern elegant pool hall, dark curtains, soft geometric ceiling lights, balanced exposure, gentle warm key light with cool blue ambient fill, realistic reflections on the green felt, shallow depth of field, natural skin texture, premium sports-fashion advertising, refined and confident mood, live-action film texture, subtle film grain.\n\nNatural realistic motion, stable hands, stable pool cue, accurate billiards table geometry.\n\nNo cuts, no shot changes, no duplicated person, no extra limbs, no distorted hands, no warped cue, no body deformation, no exaggerated curves, no flicker, no overexposure, no harsh contrast, no plastic CGI, no cartoon, no anime, no watermark, no subtitles, no random text, no logos."
